    "why": "OWNER DECISION J, ANSWERED AGAINST ITS OWN DEFAULT, AND THE CASE THAT SEPARATES THE TWO DENOMINATORS. p-ali and p-noor each hold exactly one call, on the same date, under the same one-in-two rule. p-ali is available on every day of the window and is clean; p-noor is on leave either side and is available on one day, so the allowance is zero and the single call is over. Under the calendar-day denominator the decision overrode, both windows would hold two days, both would permit one call, and neither person would be flagged — the rule TIGHTENS around leave, which is the intended and counter-intuitive half, and the explanation prints the number of available days it actually used.",
